    "recommendations": "• Remove woody debris visible near the structure, including fallen branches, wood piles, or dead material on the ground.\n\n• Thin trees in the cluster nearest the structure to create more open space between the canopy and the building.\n\n• Trim lower branches on large trees close to the structure to reduce the path fire can travel from the ground into the tree canopy.\n\n• Clear ground vegetation directly against the structure's walls and foundation.\n\n• Thin scattered shrubs near the structure to break up continuous plant material close to the building.\n\n• Keep the single access route clear of overhanging branches and ground vegetation along both edges so emergency vehicles can pass without obstruction.\n\n• Clear vegetation and debris from the rear of the structure to allow movement around the building and improve visibility for responders."
